module std.host_text

import std.types { Char, List }
import std.algebra { fold_list }
import std.nat { Nat, Zero, Succ }
import std.optional { Optional }

// THE HOST-TEXT CARRIER AND THE OPERATIONS WHOSE SEMANTICS NEED IT (operator ruling H2, 2026-10-17,
// v2-namespace-cutover). HostText is the opaque, native representation of text a host hands the
// program -- what a string literal denotes and what a target realizes as its own string type. It is
// NOT structural text: v2.std.text String is FreeMonoid<Char>, a list of Unicode scalars the language
// can fold, split and compare, and the two are distinct representations of one meaning. A host-text
// value reaches the structural carrier only through a declared crossing (chars, below) or refuses.
//
// ONE HOME, ONE NAME. HostText is never another `String`: two types of that name, one structural and
// one opaque, would keep the fork the ruling closes behind a qualifier. v2.std.node's kernel String
// is the migration-time projection of this declaration (v2.extdeps.languages.dag lists both as the
// String kernel value type) until the String-to-HostText wave respells it; that projection is not a
// second home. Only an operation that needs the host carrier lives here: equality, split, join,
// replacement and folds over text are structural and stay with structural text.
//
// SIGNATURES USE DAG-LAYER TYPES (List<Char>, from std.types). That was once forced by a tree direction
// that no longer exists (v2.std.cross_tree.import_model cross_tree_import_admitted admits a crossing between
// declared namespaces either way); it stays the right layer for a kernel carrier.
type HostText

// THE HOST-TO-STRUCTURAL CROSSING (operator ruling H4). The Unicode scalar values of the host text, in
// source order: not its bytes, not its grapheme clusters, not UTF-16 code units, and never a lossy
// decoding. A pure declared operation whose host realization binds by THIS declaration's identity
// (std.primitive_projection primitive_chars, a HostRealizedSeam row), so the body is a self-call no
// realization ever reaches -- a target without a
// realization refuses at realization, it does not fall back to a name. The inverse crossing is its own
// declared operation, text_of_chars below, not this one.
fn chars(text: HostText) -> List<Char> {
  chars(text: text)
}

// THE STRUCTURAL-TO-HOST CROSSING: THE DECLARED INVERSE OF chars (operator ruling H4; DESIGN section 4,
// ruling text_crossings_go_through_the_unfold). The host text whose Unicode scalar values, in order, are
// `scalars`, so text_of_chars(scalars: chars(text: t)) is t for every host text t, and chars of
// text_of_chars(scalars: xs) is xs for every list of scalars. Total: every Char is a Unicode scalar
// value (std.types Char), so every list has exactly one host text; a value outside that range is a
// broken representation invariant, which the realization refuses rather than dropping or substituting.
//
// NOT A SEAM, BY DECISION (tidy-ant-251, 2026-10-25): the body is the kernel's linear slice writer over
// the WHOLE list. That is a realization binding at one window, NOT an identity: chars_to_string is a
// different, windowed operation that production callers use at arbitrary windows, it clamps an
// out-of-range window and panics on a non-scalar Int, and its own authority is unestablished
// (gunbc.primitive_egress.dispositions_text, row chars_to_string). Its window [0, count) is always inside [0, count), so the writer's clamp of an
// out-of-range window never fires here, and this declaration does not rely on it. A .dag fold over
// from_code_point and concat would copy its accumulator, quadratic in the text length (DESIGN section
// 6, bare minimum cost), so the kernel writer stays the realization. It keeps its ambient name for the
// namespace wave to home; this declaration and nothing else calls it for a text crossing (std.coercion
// unicode_scalar_fold, the conversion plan's route, calls this).
fn text_of_chars(scalars: List<Char>) -> HostText {
  chars_to_string(chars: scalars, start: 0, end: scalars |> count)
}

EAD
// THE NUMBER OF UNICODE SCALAR VALUES IN HOST TEXT (G2 ruling A, condition 3, tidy-ant-251 2026-10-31):
// the length of chars(text), never its UTF-8 bytes, UTF-16 code units or grapheme clusters. Host text
// only: a site over structural text (v2.std.text String) uses std.algebra length on the list it already
// is, and the string_length wave classifies its sites by representation before any is ported. The
// answer is a Nat because a count has no negative arm.
//
// HOST-REALIZED TODAY, A SEAM BY RULING (tidy-ant-251, 2026-10-31, reversing "a .dag body"): the
// ambient primitive shadows an explicit import of this declaration, so it binds only through a
// std.primitive_projection row, and a ModeledProjection body is intercepted by the builtin arm --
// dead code that looks live, measured: a body returning Zero left every claim holding. So the
// realization binds by THIS declaration's identity (primitive_string_length, a HostRealizedSeam row)
// and no call reaches the body.
//
// THE BODY IS THE FOLD FOR ONE PR, NOT YET THE SEAM'S SELF-CALL, AND IT IS DEAD CODE. The heal job
// builds its generator from main's stage0 mirrors (claim_executor --base-mirror), and main carries no
// row for this declaration until this PR lands, so a self-call here would emit as Rust recursion
// (observed twice on this PR). The fold keeps the emitted body total meanwhile; every call routes
// through the row, so nothing executes it. Trigger: the row is on main; the follow-up PR replaces the
// body with the self-call string_length(text: text) and drops the fold's imports. Class: the
// bootstrap admission one, gunbc.recurring_failure_mode
// population_admission_compiled_into_the_comparator_refuses_a_first_time_artifact (here a roster row).
// Dissolution trigger of the seam itself: a .dag realization (this scalar-count fold over chars)
// replaces the host one once an explicit import outranks the ambient primitive.
fn string_length(text: HostText) -> Nat {
  fold_list(xs: chars(text: text), empty: Zero, cons: fn(n, _) { Succ { prev: n } })
}

// THE INDEXED READ OF A HOST TEXT, WITH ABSENCE TYPED (tidy-ant-251 ruling, 2026-11-01, the F5 row of the
// primitive-egress family). The one-code-point host text at code-point position `pos` of `text`, or Absent
// when `pos` is at or past the end. `pos` is a CODE-POINT position, never a byte offset: for the text whose
// scalars are [a, e-acute, b], position 1 is the single scalar e-acute and position 3 is Absent --
// v2.test.claim.char_at_unicode_witness measures both.
//
// ABSENCE IS TYPED, NOT INVENTED (DESIGN section 5; gunbc.recurring_failure_mode
// absence_carried_by_a_second_representation). The ambient operation refuses nothing today: it returns the
// EMPTY TEXT at or past the end and clamps a negative position to index 0, so an absent read is
// indistinguishable from an empty one and a negative position reads as the first character. This
// declaration removes both. `pos` is std.nat Nat, so a negative position is not expressible at the
// boundary, and absence is an arm of the canonical carrier std.optional.Optional (rulings
// cardinality_one_concept, dag_absence_is_one_meaning) -- not a char_at-specific sum, and not a sentinel a
// caller has to recognize.
//
// A HOST SEAM, LIKE chars ABOVE. The body is a self-call no realization reaches; the realization binds by
// THIS declaration's identity (std.primitive_projection primitive_char_at, a HostRealizedSeam row), and a
// target without that realization refuses at realization rather than falling back to a name. Its primitive
// signature already returns the Optional -- the shape of std.algebra map_lookup_primitive_delegate, whose
// body is the same self-call -- so the seam yields a declared Optional value instead of a value plus a
// special case for "nothing there".
//
// COST (DESIGN section 6, bare minimum cost). The realization is constant-time on the ASCII path and
// position-proportional on the general path (src/v1/runtime_rust.dag, v1_rt::char_at; the contract row
// std.primitives char_at_contract records work "pos" and says nothing carrier-sensitive -- making it
// carrier-sensitive is a named follow-up, not this change). A .dag body here, a guard over chars then a
// scalar read, would make every call linear and turn the per-character loops among the ambient call sites
// quadratic; src/v2/std/witness list_nth shows that shape and pays it over a list, where there is no host
// carrier to read through.
fn char_at(text: HostText, pos: Nat) -> Optional<HostText> {
  char_at(text: text, pos: pos)
}

